On Fri, 17 May 2002, Richard Adams wrote:

First off thank you very much about the kernel help. That will prove very
helpful I guess :)

> > 2)
> > I have checked out X server from cvs. Can I use cvs to track changes made
> > to spefific files/directories? I have not got so much out of "cvs log" or I
> > made something wrong.
> 
> When upgrading a kernel version you do not need to even think about changing 
> or upgrading X, if i may say so, if you need to ask howto compile a kernel on 
> a machine for another destination then i would certainly not advise you to go 
> around updating your X server.

What I meant by my question is not at all related to the kernel thing. I was
just wondering how I can use cvs to show me the changes that have been made
to certain file in my cvs checkout. For example, if some cvs comitter of
XFree86 has change a Makefile in any subdirectory, I like to know what
exactly has been done. As far as I know cvs is capable of that. And I'd also
like to know how to find files in a cvs working directory that have
"recently" been changed..

Thank you,
